# Approval policy

## Before routing
Route only when all five intake fields are valid (`intake-policy.mdc`) and the pack check passes (`research-checklist.mdc`).

## Who approves
- The requester's manager: always.
- Security: also, when intake `touches_customer_data = true` OR pack R3 shows the vendor would hold customer or personal data.
- If intake and R3 disagree, flag the mismatch and still route to Security.

## What counts as an approval
- Only an explicit decision from the named approver, recorded with their name, role, decision, timestamp, and any conditions.
- Does not count: silence, a reply from someone else, an unnamed account, a vague reply ("looks fine?"), or anything written by an agent or the bot.
- Agents and the bot never approve and never record a decision on someone's behalf.
- Each approval stores a hash of the intake fields and pack. If either changes later, the approval is cancelled (old approval and reason go to the audit log), the approver is back at `waiting`, and a new card is queued.

## Decision states
Per approver: `waiting`, `approved`, `approved_with_conditions`, `rejected`.
- Conditions are free text and carry into close-out as a checklist for the requester. The bot does not carry them out.

Overall request:
- `rejected` if any required approver rejects.
- `approved_with_conditions` if every required approver approved and at least one added conditions.
- `approved` if every required approver approved with no conditions.
- Otherwise `waiting`.

## Silence
Silence leaves the approver at `waiting`. After the configured number of hours it only triggers a nudge to that approver, logged in the audit log. The nudge routine runs a few times a day at most.

## Requester withdraw
A requester may withdraw their request at any time before the ticket is closed. A withdrawn request is closed with `final_decision = withdrawn`. The withdraw needs the requester's own words: the `--by` name and the `--reason` text. A withdrawn request is treated as closed: it appears in neither the open-ticket digest nor the status view's open count.
